2. Non-Functional Requirements
Non-functional requirements describe the quality attributes and constraints of the Company Contact Management System. They define the expected performance, usability, reliability, security, maintainability, and compatibility of the system.
2.1. Performance
   * NFR-01: The system shall display the contact list within 3 seconds under normal operating conditions.
   * NFR-02: The system shall return search results within 3 seconds under normal operating conditions.
   * NFR-03: The system shall support up to 20 concurrent users under normal operating conditions.
2.2. Usability
   * NFR-04: The system shall provide a simple and user-friendly graphical user interface (GUI).
   * NFR-05: The system shall display clear messages when an operation succeeds or fails.
2.3. Reliability
   * NFR-06: The system shall save contact information correctly and retain the saved data when the application is closed and reopened.
   * NFR-07: The system shall validate required contact information before saving it.
2.4. Security
   * NFR-08: The system shall validate user input to prevent invalid data from being saved.
   * NFR-09: The system shall ask users to confirm before deleting a contact.
   * NFR-10: The system shall restrict access to contact information and management functions according to user permissions.
2.5. Maintainability
   * NFR-11: The system shall organize its source code into separate components to make it easier to understand, modify, and maintain.
2.6. Compatibility
   * NFR-12: The system shall run on the operating systems supported by the development team.

